    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, just finished a rumenotomy on one of my heifers. need a protocol for the next few days to make sure she recovers okay. specifically what should i be looking for regarding infection and when can i start bringing her back onto feed? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A rumenotomy recovery protocol requires careful monitoring, especially for any signs of infection. You must watch for signs like fever, excessive discharge from the incision, or foul-smelling breath, which would indicate a serious issue. If the incision site looks inflamed or is oozing pus, you need to contact your veterinarian immediately. You can usually start introducing feed slowly, perhaps with a palatable, easily digestible slurry, once the initial surgical site looks stable and there are no obvious signs of severe distress. Gradual reintroduction is key to prevent further digestive upset, like a secondary bloat, which is a real risk after abdominal surgery.",
      "source": "target",
